        "node_id": "n_11_7c5de7",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of using a modified Bellman-Ford algorithm to handle negative weights and detect negative cycles is not suitable for this problem. The issue lies in the fact that the algorithm doesn't correctly count the number of shortest paths when there are negative weight edges. Instead, we should use Dijkstra's algorithm with a priority queue and keep track of the number of shortest paths to each vertex. This approach will work correctly for graphs with non-negative edge weights, which is the case for this problem.",
